{{!
    @template mod_vrroom/panorama_picker

    The body of the direction picker (mod_vrroom/panorama_picker): the flat 360° photo with a
    crosshair on the chosen direction. Clicking the photo moves the crosshair; so do the arrow keys
    (Shift for bigger steps); Enter uses the direction.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none (the elements are found by id: {{id}}, {{id}}-mark, {{id}}-value)

    Context variables required for this template:
    * id - unique id of the picking area
    * url - URL of the photo

    Example context (json):
    {
        "id": "vrroom-pick-1",
        "url": "https://example.com/pluginfile.php/1/user/draft/2/photo.jpg"
    }
}}
<p class="small mb-2" id="{{id}}-help">{{#str}}panoramapickerhelp, mod_vrroom{{/str}}</p>
<div class="vrroom-panopicker position-relative" id="{{id}}" tabindex="0" role="application"
     aria-label="{{#str}}panoramapickertitle, mod_vrroom{{/str}}" aria-describedby="{{id}}-help {{id}}-value">
    <img class="vrroom-panopicker-image d-block w-100 rounded" src="{{url}}" alt="" draggable="false">
    <span class="vrroom-panopicker-mark" id="{{id}}-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
</div>
<p class="small text-body-secondary mt-2 mb-0" id="{{id}}-value" aria-live="polite"></p>
